    "assessment": {
      "scope": "Selected original2016 RIVM report, independently identified LC-IMPACT land chapter and2020 journal PDF, with previously qualified ReCiPe2017 journal evidence. These are distinct works/carriers; the2016 report is not the2017v1.1 report and a method-portal link does not qualify a factor archive. Shared recovery literature is not independent empirical confirmation.",
      "relation": "The original ReCiPe land midpoint already incorporates passive recovery duration. Its positive fixed land conversion includes model density/reference assumptions and preserves ordering within compatible category results, but adds no excluded years or new causal step and cannot convert to the LC global indicator. LC Equation11.18 counts the first100 post-abandonment years along the original recovery, including a nonzero late branch, rather than accelerating recovery or scaling by elapsed-time fraction.",
      "derivation": "The book uses one specified unweighted regional occupation factor c in species/m2 and matching T. Integrating the stated linear representation to u=min(H,T) gives c*(u-u*u/(2*T)) in regional species*year/m2, then physical area is applied. Later vulnerability/taxon aggregation has its own global scale. H generalization and T=2H, short/zero/signed and heterogeneous-duration checks are authored algebra, not published arbitrary-horizon factors or measured restoration.",
      "limits": "Nonnegative bounds are not applied to negative or uncertain summaries. Independent quantiles do not determine a tail quantile without corresponding joint information. The original2016 pasture/annual-crop printed discrepancy and the LC robustness parenthesis remain explicit; no official correction, uninspected workbook, software behavior, extinction count or ecological recovery is inferred.",
      "conservation": "All917 preceding claims, old catalog sources/evidence and their relative order retain identity. Ten new claims, nine evidence records and three original-source readings support B14. The old six B14 claims and three headings remain; the existing RIVM work metadata and old article access limitation receive bounded dated updates while original discovery, identity, artifacts and passages are protected. No case, registry or dependency changes.",
      "review": "Fresh source/design and exact draft/canonical assessments led to units, time origin, conditional mathematics and source-role corrections. The canonical source closure binds7e6dca1; the final80d03e6 restores the already-supported global PDF unit gloss, checked by the primary agent and independent reader. Pure structure checks and private exact-fraction controls are separate from scientific and human-expert validity."
